ef 17592186260820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262547 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262547 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262547 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262547 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262547 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186260339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262547 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f46674a6-7e2b-5656-b018-7f5bf5e7afa0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262855 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186262177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262855 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127936" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262855 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262855 #edb/ref 1071 "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(3,-2,5)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(-3,0,2)$ and $B(2,1,3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262855 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "57b46f7d-b75a-5f5c-87e6-c8948d671ea4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262855 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,-2,5⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(-3,0,2)$ and $B(2,1,3)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,1,3⟩-⟨-3,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨5,1,1⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩ & =⟨3,-2,5⟩\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩ & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336721 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336721 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336721 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4ad3af79-fcd3-5749-b0e5-9411379a50d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337264 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337264 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337264 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "886c099c-bd36-506a-9021-b550fe0b57c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337364 #edb/ref 1080 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337364 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337364 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "926d8af8-a19c-5443-bbf7-6f269886e17b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337896 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337896 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337896 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d60f66f3-48fa-5ebf-837a-e090ca7d3d6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337925 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337925 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186337925 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d99cfee8-de55-5ea6-8c2e-3385468433bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338483 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338483 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338483 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186337896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338483 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7727c896-6f1b-5615-b00c-42ad7fd27f9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338831 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338831 #edb/ref 1069 "q-70830" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338831 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338831 #edb/ref 1071 "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,-3⟩=8.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338831 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e0327785-b28b-5842-b652-0805899123b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338831 #edb/ref 1074 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,-3⟩=8$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-1,1,-3⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,1,-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ -{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}-3{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & ={t}_{1}+3{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{1}+3{t}_{3},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393029 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393029 #edb/ref 1069 "q-70827" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393029 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393029 #edb/ref 1071 "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨1,2,-1⟩=7.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393029 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ee04e6aa-94ba-5e6d-a904-4a34aac7a757" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393029 #edb/ref 1074 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨1,2,-1⟩=7$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨1,2,-1⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2,-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ {t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}-{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{3} & ={t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{2},\\,{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{2}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{2}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{1}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393030 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393030 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393030 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393030 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393030 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393030 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393030 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393030 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186393032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393030 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b14d7746-5f36-5ef0-9936-be22c8877f39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393031 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393031 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393031 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c4fb71df-948c-5126-86b0-9d79cb4c0fee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393032 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393032 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393032 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "75ed4713-5dc0-5929-8f1a-ae29368dccf9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393033 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393033 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393033 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "14d6c7a2-54c1-5ce2-9906-4d55cf87f498" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393034 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393034 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393034 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "32938842-cdd7-5118-b60e-0c5d24a27836" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393035 #edb/ref 1